message: "If you use this work or reference this project, please cite the paper below."
title: "Development of a Real-Time Multi-Modal Sensor for Field-Based Microplastic Detection"
abstract: >-
  GangaDrishthi is a compact, low-cost system that fuses impedance spectroscopy,
  programmable multispectral optical imaging, and YOLOv8 deep-learning microscopy
  for rapid, on-site microplastic detection in water. It classifies polymer type,
  estimates particle size, and produces a geo-tagged Microplastic Risk Index (MRI),
  delivering laboratory-grade accuracy in the field.
